Finally, the very first implementation of the plugin system.
Behind the scenes me and @mcollina worked hard to achieve the following features:
- Plugin encapsulation
- Plugin Inheritance
- Asynchronous plugin load
- Dependency management

There is still lot of work to do, such as find nicer names for the apis, think about a better system for dependency handling (name and version?) and if we want to expose some internals to the plugins.

We also need to figure out how can we add methods to `Request` and `Reply` as well (we not necessarily have to do it in this PR).

Example:
```js
const fastify = require('fastify')()

// register provides encapsulation
fastify.register((instance, opts, next) => {
  // plugin do the same work of register, but without encapsulation
  instance.plugin((i, o, n) => {
    i.addServerMethod('test', 'first')
    n()
  })

  instance.get('/first', (req, reply) => {
    // this will always send { plugin: 'first' }
    reply.send({ plugin: instance.test })
  })

  next()
})

fastify.register((instance, opts, next) => {
  // even if they have the same name, the two plugins does not overwrite each other
  instance.plugin((i, o, n) => {
    i.addServerMethod('test', 'second')
    n()
  })

  instance.get('/second', (req, reply) => {
    // this will always send { plugin: 'second' }
    reply.send({ plugin: instance.test })
  })

  next()
})

fastify.listen(3000, err => {
  if (err) throw err
})
```
