**Why this PR?**
Have `onRequest` and `onResponse` with different signature and objects leads to confusion and slightly complex internals, this pr fixes that.

**What changes?**
`onRequest` will have the same objects as `preHandler`, the difference is that the `body` has not been parsed yet.
`onResponse` will also get the full request object (which could be useful) and the reply object.
Middlewares will continue to use the Node core objects.

```js
  fastify.addHook('onRequest', function (request, reply, next) {
    // request and reply are the core Fastify objects
    next()
  })

  fastify.addHook('onResponse', function (request, reply, next) {
	// request and reply are the core Fastify objects
    next()
  })

  fastify.use(function (req, res, next) {
    // req and res are the Node core objects
    next()
  })
```

This is a *breaking change*, so if accepted it will land in the next semver major.

