 This PR is a follow on to issue #3391. The PR provides a working prototype for a possible future plugin system to allow third party type inference libraries to interface fastify's type definitions. The implementation specifically focuses on setting up the necessary types to enable such a system, as well as implements the type provider mechanism mentioned on #3391. This with the goal of enabling automatic static type inference in the Fastify project.

## Type Providers

This implementation adds an additional function to the Fastify API. This function accepts a single generic argument of type FastifyTypeProvider. The type (an HKT) can be thought of as a mapping function that accepts the input of one type and maps it to another The current implementation is setup to pass user defined request schema as inputs, which are in turn made accessible for auxiliary type inference.

The following demonstrates usage with the TypeBox and Json-Schema-To-Ts libraries.

### TypeBox

```typescript
import Fastify, { FastifyTypeProvider } from 'fastify'

import { Static } from '@sinclair/typebox'

// setup

interface TypeBoxProvider extends FastifyTypeProvider { output: Static<this["input"]> }

const fastify = Fastify().typeProvider<TypeBoxProvider>()

// usage

fastify.get('/', {
    schema: {
        body: Type.Object({
            a: Type.String(),
            b: Type.Number(),
            c: Type.Boolean()
        }),
    }
}, (req, res) => {
    req.body.a // a = string
    req.body.b // b = number
    req.body.c // c = boolean
})

```
### Json-Schema-to-Ts

```typescript

import Fastify, { FastifyTypeProvider } from 'fastify'

import { FromSchema } from 'json-schema-to-ts'

// setup

interface JsonSchemaProvider extends FastifyTypeProvider { output: FromSchema<this["input"]> }

const fastify = instance.typeProvider<JsonSchemaProvider>()

// usage

fastify.get('/', {
    schema: {
        body: {
            type: 'object',
            properties: {
                a: { type: 'string' },
                b: { type: 'number' },
                c: { type: 'boolean' }
            },

        } as const
    }
}, (req, res) => {
